1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:05,660
You like me as a friend, right?

2
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:06,610
What do you think?

3
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:08,890
Something good happen?

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:11,000
You kept your bed hair intact.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,400
Mayama, you've become best buds with Asamiya.

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,640
Smells like Asamiya.

7
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,600
What do you think of him?

8
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,250
I guess he feels far away?

9
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,690
If Asamiya feels so far, then get close!

10
00:00:25,690 --> 00:00:29,510
You only "like" me as a friend, right?

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:31,270
Of course not.

12
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:33,480
We took it too far. Sorry!

13
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:36,350
Can we be friends, too?

14
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:38,280
- Huh?
- Let's join the planning committee.

15
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:39,440
Planning committee?

16
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:41,440
Brilliant idea.

17
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,800
You weren't put off by the idea?

18
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:47,730
I hope we didn't force you
onto the planning committee.

19
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:50,370
Asamiya's "like"

20
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:53,950
was not as a friend.

21
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:57,140
A guy like Asamiya

22
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,270
is way out of my league.

23
00:01:10,530 --> 00:01:13,170
A haunted house!

24
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:24,180
The results are in.
Our class will be doing...

25
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:27,900
a haunted house for the culture festival!

26
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:44,020
- That was a close poll.
- For sure.

27
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:47,420
- Too bad our butler cafe idea didn't win.
- Yeah.

28
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:51,040
<i>If anything...</i>

29
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,990
Welcome home, milady.

30
00:01:58,230 --> 00:02:01,540
<i>I thought it had plenty of potential.</i>

31
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,580
I guess it ultimately works out, though.

32
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:06,760
Asamiya prefers to work backstage anyway.

33
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:10,020
Yeah, our cafe would hinge
on him working up front.

34
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:13,070
I bet Mayama wanted to see
Asamiya's butler fit, too.

35
00:02:13,070 --> 00:02:15,140
No, I...

36
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:19,200
<i>Yes, I voted for the butler cafe. Sorry.</i>

37
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:21,970
I'd dress up for Mayama.

38
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:27,580
Anyway, I'll be working backstage
for the haunted house as well.

39
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,890
Sure thing.

40
00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:32,780
Maybe we can shop for costumes this weekend?

41
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:37,110
Yeah, we'll need fits for our various scares.

42
00:02:37,110 --> 00:02:41,140
Mayama, hope you're ready
to spook our guests.

43
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:43,710
Sure, I'll do my best.

44
00:02:44,610 --> 00:02:45,740
I'm hyped.

45
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:48,360
Same. What should I dress as?

46
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:41,780
How do I look?

47
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,300
Stylish.

48
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,420
Thanks for the clothes.

49
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,920
My little brother,
hanging out with friends...

50
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:53,040
I'm glad we picked the farther away school.

51
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,970
We're just grabbing supplies together.

52
00:03:54,970 --> 00:03:59,160
I'm more surprised
you wanted a proper outfit.

53
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,430
Let me guess.

54
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:03,620
There's someone in the group
who catches your eye?

55
00:04:05,910 --> 00:04:10,090
Just kidding. I know it's an all-boys school.

56
00:04:10,090 --> 00:04:11,590
Yeah.

57
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:17,250
<i>You only "like" me</i>

58
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:19,060
<i>as a friend, right?</i>

59
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:22,080
<i>Like you "like" everyone else.</i>

60
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:25,300
Of course not.

61
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,610
Hare?

62
00:04:27,610 --> 00:04:29,560
We're just going shopping.

63
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,120
I know.

64
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:34,320
- So are you good on time?
- Huh?

65
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:36,770
Crap. See you later!

66
00:04:36,770 --> 00:04:38,550
Have fun!

67
00:04:57,970 --> 00:04:59,900
Just made it.

68
00:05:07,180 --> 00:05:08,810
Mayama.

69
00:05:20,970 --> 00:05:23,240
Something wrong?

70
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:26,770
Sorry. You just look... different, today.

71
00:05:26,770 --> 00:05:27,850
Do I really?

72
00:05:27,850 --> 00:05:29,900
Uh, I mean...

73
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:31,830
Where's Sakaki and Tsunekawada?

74
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:36,150
They're running late.
They went to grab some props first.

75
00:05:36,150 --> 00:05:37,820
I see.

76
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:42,610
Your clothes make you look older.

77
00:05:42,610 --> 00:05:44,370
Is that weird?

78
00:05:44,370 --> 00:05:48,310
These are my brother's,
so they're a bit baggy.

79
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:49,480
You have a brother?

80
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,990
No need to be so uptight about it.

81
00:05:51,990 --> 00:05:56,030
But, yeah. I never know what to wear, so...

82
00:05:59,470 --> 00:06:00,870
Huh?

83
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:05,410
- Let's at least roll up your pant legs.
- Sure.

84
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:22,380
And one more thing.

85
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:26,020
Since your outfit has a mature flare to it...

86
00:06:31,070 --> 00:06:33,400
You should part your bangs.

87
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,960
Yeah, looks good.

88
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:41,880
The clothes are wearing me, aren't they?

89
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:43,830
That's not true.

90
00:06:43,830 --> 00:06:45,380
Huh?

91
00:06:46,430 --> 00:06:50,270
Be more confident in yourself.

92
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:56,510
- Hey there.
- Thanks for waiting.

93
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:58,660
No way.

94
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:00,340
Asamiya's on time for once.

95
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:01,630
I can't believe it.

96
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:04,990
He's either late, or straight up ditches
when he's got plans with us.

97
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:06,540
- Really?
- Yeah.

98
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:09,670
I'd never keep Mayama waiting.

99
00:07:09,670 --> 00:07:11,680
Wow.

100
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,770
The power of Mayama.

101
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:15,600
Let's go.

102
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:18,010
Dang.

103
00:07:18,010 --> 00:07:21,420
Asamiya, you're scaring me, dude.

104
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:22,700
Seriously.

105
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:24,360
It's all Mayama, I guess.

106
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:26,980
So, where do we start?

107
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:29,340
Any outfit ideas?

108
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:32,920
- We got great weather today.
- Yeah.

109
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,720
Who's outfit do we look for first?

110
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:38,030
Let's start with Mayama's costume.

111
00:07:38,030 --> 00:07:39,150
Sounds good.

112
00:07:39,150 --> 00:07:42,450
Maybe we'll find the rest along the way.

113
00:07:45,050 --> 00:07:47,580
Does that always happen?

114
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:51,370
Only whenever Asamiya's around.

115
00:07:51,370 --> 00:07:53,000
- They're not squealing at me?
- No.

116
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,500
For real?

117
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:58,710
- I thought I was popular.
- They clearly only care about Asamiya.

118
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:00,300
Seriously?

119
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,420
- Bummer...
- Cheer up, man.

120
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:06,720
Fuzzy ears?

121
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:09,120
What for?

122
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:12,500
After a heated back and forth discussion,

123
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:14,970
we agreed you'd be a werewolf.

124
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:17,600
Yeah. Try them on.

125
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:28,210
Not exactly what we imagined.

126
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:32,020
He's not scary, that's for sure.

127
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:33,530
Any thoughts, Asamiya?

128
00:08:33,530 --> 00:08:35,290
He looks cute.

129
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:40,220
Werewolves aren't supposed to be cute, right?

130
00:08:41,030 --> 00:08:45,910
No, it could work.

131
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:48,130
Agreed.

132
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:50,950
I'll find an outfit for you.

133
00:08:52,530 --> 00:08:55,000
Asamiya's fired up about this.

134
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:59,670
Wish he'd brought that enthusiasm
when he first joined our committee.

135
00:09:01,150 --> 00:09:04,740
Well, Asamiya can handle Mayama's outfit.

136
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:06,250
Let's go find something for ourselves.

137
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:07,730
Sure.

138
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:17,200
Which one will you start with?

139
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:34,870
Huh?

140
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:37,760
You all right in there?

141
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:42,080
I'm having trouble with this choker.

142
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,750
Hold on.

143
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,460
Huh?

144
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:52,030
Wait, what?

145
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:56,270
Asamiya?

146
00:09:56,270 --> 00:09:58,180
Hold still.

147
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:08,520
There.

148
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:10,460
Thanks.

149
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,950
Perfect.

150
00:10:21,030 --> 00:10:23,200
Sir?

151
00:10:25,190 --> 00:10:27,060
Scare you?

152
00:10:32,050 --> 00:10:35,030
[Stickout, Used Clothing]

153
00:10:46,450 --> 00:10:49,190
Sakaki and Tsunekawada need more time.

154
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:51,080
All right.

155
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,410
Let's ditch them.

156
00:10:52,410 --> 00:10:53,860
Huh?

157
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:56,570
Come on.

158
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:18,950
Vanilla, or twist. Which one?

159
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:21,950
I'll take whatever you don't pick.

160
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:23,690
You okay with vanilla?

161
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,660
Yeah, thanks.

162
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:35,430
I hope they don't mind that we left.

163
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:38,400
Want a bite?

164
00:11:39,930 --> 00:11:42,400
Hurry, before it melts.

165
00:11:45,170 --> 00:11:46,700
Okay.

166
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:55,400
It's good.

167
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:57,100
Right?

168
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:13,650
It was melting.

169
00:12:27,170 --> 00:12:30,380
Anywhere you want to go? We've got time.

170
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,450
I'll leave it up to you.

171
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:38,110
I want to go where you want to go.

172
00:12:38,750 --> 00:12:43,550
I didn't have anywhere in mind...

173
00:12:48,870 --> 00:13:00,520
[Kosokodo - Used bookstore]

174
00:13:15,010 --> 00:13:16,780
A bookstore?

175
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:21,780
Yeah. It's an out-of-the-way place for me.

176
00:13:23,650 --> 00:13:25,610
I didn't know you liked to read.

177
00:13:25,610 --> 00:13:28,830
I only read a book a month.

178
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,250
I learned something new today.

179
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:36,090
What about you? Do you read?

180
00:13:36,090 --> 00:13:39,870
If it's a hobby of yours, I'll give it a try.

181
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,750
Give me a recommendation.

182
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:53,310
Sure.

183
00:13:53,310 --> 00:13:56,460
Let's see...

184
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:08,950
How about this one?

185
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:13,570
Sure.

186
00:14:15,140 --> 00:14:17,730
You're not going to read the summary?

187
00:14:17,730 --> 00:14:19,650
I'll take this one.

188
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:23,050
That'll be 820 yen.

189
00:14:24,830 --> 00:14:26,480
Let me get your change.

190
00:14:27,910 --> 00:14:29,550
- Mayama.
- Yeah?

191
00:14:33,090 --> 00:14:35,380
They're giving out freebies.

192
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:37,700
Really?

193
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:39,800
[Aoba Publishing Fair]

194
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:42,310
There are four designs in total.

195
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,320
May I have this one?

196
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:45,880
Sure thing.

197
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:51,430
Your change of 180 yen,

198
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:54,630
and your book.

199
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:01,530
Thank you, come again.

200
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,530
- Here.
- Huh?

201
00:15:04,530 --> 00:15:06,350
You can have it.

202
00:15:06,350 --> 00:15:08,780
Perfect for the name, "Hare", right?
[T/N: "Hare" means "sunny day"]

203
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:13,070
Thanks.

204
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:16,150
Give me a sec to browse, too.

205
00:15:18,990 --> 00:15:22,840
Sorry, my phone was out of battery.

206
00:15:23,490 --> 00:15:26,080
Sounds good.

207
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,280
Thanks for waiting.

208
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:34,090
Perfect timing. Sakaki and Tsunekawada
also just finished.

209
00:15:34,090 --> 00:15:35,990
Sorry I took a while.

210
00:15:35,990 --> 00:15:38,100
I hadn't visited in a minute,

211
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:40,580
so I couldn't stop browsing.

212
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:45,370
It's fine. I had fun seeing you so excited.

213
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:48,250
Asamiya.

214
00:15:49,450 --> 00:15:50,960
Here.

215
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,540
This one's for you.

216
00:15:57,220 --> 00:16:01,290
Your first name, "Kosei",
means "shining star", right?

217
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:03,030
So, yeah.

218
00:16:11,290 --> 00:16:15,720
Our first date, and your first gift.

219
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,800
I could die today.

220
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:20,870
That's seriously not funny.

221
00:16:20,870 --> 00:16:22,910
But you won't deny the "date" part.

222
00:16:22,910 --> 00:16:26,080
What? No, well...

223
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:30,290
That's because there was lots more to rag on.

224
00:16:32,190 --> 00:16:34,330
Sure, I'll leave it at that.

225
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:40,080
Thanks.

226
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:43,050
That's what I should be saying.

227
00:16:43,050 --> 00:16:45,760
I had fun today. Thanks.

228
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:47,510
You have any plans after this?

229
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:50,420
I have to finish up some homework.

230
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:53,160
- Makes sense.
- Don't you?

231
00:16:53,160 --> 00:16:54,720
I already finished everything.

232
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,810
I'm not surprised.

233
00:16:55,810 --> 00:16:57,790
Well, I only did everything

234
00:16:57,790 --> 00:17:00,420
because I wanted to leave the day free.

235
00:17:01,950 --> 00:17:03,920
Kosei?

236
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:06,500
Hey, it's been a while!

237
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:09,010
You're as good-looking as ever.

238
00:17:09,010 --> 00:17:10,180
What's up?

239
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:12,560
I'm out shopping.

240
00:17:13,270 --> 00:17:15,060
Who's this?

241
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:17,130
A friend from high school.

242
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:20,310
I see.

243
00:17:25,340 --> 00:17:27,540
She's a classmate from middle school.

244
00:17:42,580 --> 00:17:45,750
Thanks for walking me home.

245
00:17:48,550 --> 00:17:51,190
You live pretty far from school.

246
00:17:51,190 --> 00:17:53,820
How about I come get you every morning?

247
00:17:53,820 --> 00:17:56,220
Uh, well...

248
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:57,750
Should I not?

249
00:17:59,950 --> 00:18:01,620
Yeah, please don't.

250
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:07,640
Asamiya.

251
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:09,100
You and I are...

252
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:11,440
Welcome home, Hare.

253
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:12,530
Tenn?

254
00:18:12,530 --> 00:18:15,230
- Your brother...
- Oh, hey!

255
00:18:15,230 --> 00:18:20,120
Is this the friend you went out with today?

256
00:18:21,140 --> 00:18:24,150
My name is Kosei Asamiya.
It's an honor to meet you.

257
00:18:24,150 --> 00:18:26,860
I'm Tenn Mayama, Hare's older brother.

258
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:30,680
It's nice to see Hare bring someone over.

259
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,430
- Is that unusual?
- Yeah.

260
00:18:32,430 --> 00:18:35,090
It might honestly be a first.

261
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:37,040
How about it? Wanna come in?

262
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:39,270
It's fine. He just walked me home.

263
00:18:39,270 --> 00:18:42,630
He walked you home?

264
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:45,720
I mean...

265
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,290
<i>Right, that's weird.</i>

266
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:51,000
<i>Why would a guy walk another guy home?</i>

267
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,600
I walked him back,
because I worry he's too cute.

268
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:56,530
A-Asamiya?

269
00:18:56,530 --> 00:18:58,710
- I totally get you.
- Huh?

270
00:18:58,710 --> 00:19:02,020
My brother's just the cutest.

271
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:05,410
He's started to get
a bit prickly around me, though.

272
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:07,540
- Really?
- Yeah.

273
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:11,190
Just the other day,
I tried to fix his bed hair,

274
00:19:11,190 --> 00:19:13,210
but he refused my help!

275
00:19:13,210 --> 00:19:14,820
- Cute.
- Right?

276
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:19,220
Say, can we trade numbers?

277
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:20,680
Of course.

278
00:19:25,310 --> 00:19:27,570
<i>These two...</i>

279
00:19:27,570 --> 00:19:29,670
<i>They're the picture perfect pair.</i>

280
00:19:31,430 --> 00:19:34,180
Crap, I have a job to get to.

281
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:35,920
Hope you visit again, Asamiya.

282
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:38,800
I will, thank you.

283
00:19:44,030 --> 00:19:46,180
He's a nice guy.

284
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:48,800
You two are nothing alike, though.

285
00:19:52,570 --> 00:19:56,790
You can say that again.

286
00:19:56,790 --> 00:19:58,260
Huh?

287
00:20:00,250 --> 00:20:03,260
My brother is amazing.

288
00:20:04,050 --> 00:20:07,980
He's tall, popular,

289
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:10,360
and talented, too.

290
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,500
But, I'm...

291
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:26,270
<i>His brother is so talented.</i>

292
00:20:26,270 --> 00:20:29,630
- <i>He's smart, athletic...</i>
- <i>Right?</i>

293
00:20:29,630 --> 00:20:31,000
<i>It's such a wonder.</i>

294
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,220
<i>How are they related?</i>

295
00:20:38,150 --> 00:20:40,340
Mayama?

296
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:43,260
Never mind. It's nothing.

297
00:20:44,670 --> 00:20:46,930
It's clearly not, "nothing". What's up?

298
00:20:53,620 --> 00:20:56,340
When you confessed to me,

299
00:20:57,310 --> 00:21:01,130
I think I was happy.

300
00:21:03,650 --> 00:21:08,100
You're kind, and fun to hang out with.

301
00:21:08,790 --> 00:21:11,000
I promise, that's no lie.

302
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:14,520
It's just...

303
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:22,500
There are better people out there for you.

304
00:21:24,930 --> 00:21:29,430
But I like 'you', Mayama.

305
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:32,180
Why?

306
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:39,400
I'm a boring guy.

307
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:41,600
There's nothing special about me.

308
00:21:43,710 --> 00:21:46,410
So why me?

309
00:21:49,190 --> 00:21:51,200
Because you're you.

310
00:21:57,310 --> 00:21:59,920
That's not an answer.

311
00:22:11,950 --> 00:22:16,060
<i>Why do I like him so much?</i>

312
00:22:25,790 --> 00:22:29,340
Here. Have this last one.

313
00:22:29,340 --> 00:22:31,420
- You sure?
- Yeah.

314
00:22:31,420 --> 00:22:32,880
Here you go.

315
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:34,390
Thank you.

316
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:36,660
I'll always have some in stock.

317
00:22:36,660 --> 00:22:38,170
Good to know.

318
00:22:40,870 --> 00:22:43,650
<i>But I'm sure about one thing.</i>

319
00:22:46,530 --> 00:22:49,560
<i>Mayama is my first real crush.</i>

320
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:16,330
I don't know how I should treat you anymore.

321
00:24:16,330 --> 00:24:20,490
I've never worked in a group
with friends before.

322
00:24:20,490 --> 00:24:22,340
I want our haunted house to be a success.

323
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:25,040
I would find myself
looking at Mayama from afar.

324
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:27,470
It didn't take long for me to realize

325
00:24:27,470 --> 00:24:29,650
what I felt for him now, was "love".

326
00:24:29,650 --> 00:24:30,900
Why do you want to go out with me?

327
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:32,810
We saw the video.
Can we get a selfie together?

328
00:24:32,810 --> 00:24:34,170
These comments are nasty.

329
00:24:34,170 --> 00:24:37,180
People always took one look at me,
and made assumptions.

330
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:40,130
Don't use me as engagement bait.

331
00:24:40,130 --> 00:24:42,280
He's just a shallow guy with the looks.

332
00:24:42,280 --> 00:24:45,440
If I posted a shot of Asamiya in a dress,
I'd get crazy likes.

333
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:47,810
I don't think Asamiya would appreciate that.

334
00:24:47,810 --> 00:24:49,950
Asamiya's feelings matter.

335
00:24:49,950 --> 00:24:53,320
Sorry. I kept saying I liked you,

336
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:57,570
without even considering how you felt.

